# AdinKhepra ASAF Engine — Cursor Rules
# Place this file at: giza-cyber-shield/.cursorrules

## Project identity

AdinKhepra is the security camera AND the flight recorder for AI agents.

Security camera: watches what AI agents do in real time, alerts on anomalies.
Flight recorder: creates a permanent, tamper-proof record that proves what
happened — for auditors, forensics, compliance, and incident response.

Never describe this product using the words "cryptographic attestation" without
immediately adding plain-English translation. "Permanently records and signs every
AI action so it can't be denied or altered" is always better than "cryptographic
attestation framework."

## Core architecture rules

Go + Next.js/TypeScript monorepo. Single static binary output. Zero CGO. No
external AI API dependencies in core engine. All AI provider calls are isolated
to pkg/g0dm0d3/ only.

The DAG (pkg/dag/) is sacred. Every significant operation writes a signed node.
Use dag.GlobalDAG() — never instantiate a new Memory directly.

## What I'm building right now

1. pkg/asaf/wrapper.go — MCP interceptor that wraps any AI agent transparently
2. CLI simplification — fewer commands, cleaner surface
3. VPS deployment to root@187.124.225.91
4. G0DM0D3 provider abstraction (Anthropic/OpenRouter/Offline, no Ollama needed)

## Build commands

Development: go build -o bin/adinkhepra.exe ./cmd/adinkhepra
Linux VPS: GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o bin/adinkhepra-linux-amd64 ./cmd/adinkhepra
Deploy: scp bin/adinkhepra-linux-amd64 root@187.124.225.91:/opt/adinkhepra/bin/adinkhepra && ssh root@187.124.225.91 "systemctl restart adinkhepra"

## Security invariants — never break these

- CGO_ENABLED=0 always
- No external AI API calls outside pkg/g0dm0d3/
- No plaintext secrets on disk
- master_seed.sealed lives at ~/.asaf/keys/ never in project root
- Dilithium3 sign every DAG node
- FIPS 203/204/205 only for new crypto features
- Return errors, never panic() in production paths

## Code conventions

Go error format: fmt.Errorf("FunctionName: %w", err)
Logging: use pkg/logging/dod_logger.go, never fmt.Println
DAG write functions: prefix with Record (RecordSTIGFinding, RecordAgentAction)
ASAF wrappers: prefix with Wrap (WrapMCPAgent, WrapHTTPAgent)
Function max size: 60 lines before splitting

## Accurate product facts — never change these

Patent: USPTO #73565085
Signing algorithm: Dilithium3 (NIST FIPS 204 / ML-DSA)
KEM algorithm: Kyber-1024 (NIST FIPS 203 / ML-KEM)
Compliance mappings: 36,195
Company: SecRed Knowledge Inc. (NouchiX)
Product name: AdinKhepra (capital A, capital K, one word)
Framework: ASAF — Agentic Security Attestation Framework
Founder: SGT Souhimbou "Cyber" Doh Kone, SDVOSB

## The demo we're always building toward

User runs `adinkhepra watch`, uses Claude Code for 5 minutes, opens
http://localhost:45444, sees signed tamper-proof record of every AI action.
"That's what an auditor sees. Can you show them this without us?" That's the close.
